          "checkable_at": "Fiscal Q3 2026 Form 10-Q."
        }
      ],
      "what_must_be_true": "Record B2B bookings must convert into shipments without meaningful cancellations, Industrial utilization and data-center Communications mix must sustain GAAP gross-margin expansion, and Automotive must stabilize rather than offset the Industrial recovery. ADI also needs to preserve roughly 49% adjusted operating margin while funding R&D and keeping working-capital absorption temporary."
    },
    "preview_note": "ADI enters fiscal Q3 with unusually strong momentum: fiscal Q2 revenue rose 37% year over year, Industrial increased 56%, Communications increased 79%, and management cited record B2B bookings. I forecast $4.02 billion of revenue, modestly above the $4.00 billion top of guidance, and $3.44 of adjusted EPS versus the guided $3.30 midpoint. The principal upside drivers are continued Industrial restocking and AI-related data-center demand; the key offsets are uneven Automotive demand, tougher sequential comparisons and a meaningful working-capital build as ADI supports higher shipments. I expect GAAP gross margin to reach 68.2% and adjusted operating leverage to carry earnings above guidance. The reaction should depend less on a small Q3 beat than on whether fiscal Q4 guidance confirms revenue above $4 billion with adjusted EPS near $3.50. Cash conversion is the secondary watch item: my $1.28 billion FCF estimate assumes the Q2 working-capital outflow begins to normalize but does not fully reverse.",
    "reasoning": "The forecast starts from fiscal Q2 revenue of approximately $3.623 billion, GAAP gross margin of 67.3%, adjusted operating margin of 49.0% and adjusted EPS of $3.09. The attached end-market visual confirms a 15% sequential revenue increase in Q2, led by 20% Industrial and 22% Communications growth, while Automotive rose 8% and Consumer was flat. Filed commentary attributes the expansion to broad Industrial demand, especially test equipment and aerospace/defense, plus AI-driven data-center infrastructure. I therefore place Q3 revenue 3% above the $3.9 billion guidance midpoint. Higher utilization and favorable mix lift GAAP gross margin to 68.2%, but variable compensation and continued R&D investment limit incremental operating leverage. The adjusted-EPS bridge uses the company's projected $391 million acquisition-related adjustment and $51 million associated tax effect. Cash flow assumes strong earnings and non-cash amortization are partly offset by a $450 million working-capital use as receivables and inventory support higher sales. The longer-range path assumes the current cyclical recovery moderates into high-single-digit structural growth, with gross-margin durability, disciplined capital spending and substantial shareholder distributions."
  },
